        "original_id": "273ce541-9db2-5cdf-9030-efc79b4c4ac8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chuck Brodsky, Moe Berg\n- Topics: Songwriting themes, Baseball, Espionage, World War II\n- Works: \"The Ballad of Eddie Klepp\", \"Moe Berg: The Song\", \"Doc Ellis' No-No\"\n- Organizations: Major League Baseball, Office of Strategic Services\n\nFacts:\n- Morris \"Moe\" Berg was born on March 2, 1902.\n- Moe Berg was an American catcher and coach in Major League Baseball.\n- During World War II, Moe Berg served as a spy for the Office of Strategic Services.\n- Chuck Brodsky is particularly known for often humorous and political lyrics.\n- Chuck Brodsky is also known for baseball songs such as \"The Ballad of Eddie Klepp\", \"Moe Berg: The Song\", and \"Doc Ellis' No-No\".\n- Moe Berg died on May 29, 1972.",
